    "chunk_size_bytes": 1507,
    "chunk_text": "Lankan Scout leader Bhanuka Karunaratne first to receive Japan\u2019s Wood Badge\n\nBhanuka Karunaratne has made scouting history by becoming the first Sri Lankan to be awarded the Wood Badge, the highest international training recognition for Scout leaders, in Japan.\n\nThe prestigious honour was formally presented during a Board of Directors meeting of the Scout Association of Japan in Hyogo Prefecture.\n\nThe Wood Badge is regarded as one of the most distinguished training awards in the global scouting movement and is conferred on leaders who demonstrate advanced leadership and team-building skills, strong instructional ability, and a deep understanding of scouting principles.\n\nTo earn the qualification, Karunaratne completed a rigorous series of theoretical and practical training modules approved by the Scout Association of Japan, designed to develop high-level competencies in scout leadership.\n\nThe Wood Badge is an internationally recognised symbol of excellence in scouting, reflecting a commitment to youth development and leadership training.\n\nAn alumnus of Kingswood College, Kandy, Karunaratne\u2019s achievement has been hailed as a milestone for Sri Lanka\u2019s scouting movement, bringing recognition to the country on the international stage and serving as an inspiration to scouts across the island.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
