    "chunk_size_bytes": 1936,
    "chunk_text": "LANKATILES opens 60th showroom in Colombo\n\nLANKATILES has strengthened its retail footprint with the opening of its 60th showroom in Sri Lanka, marking a significant milestone in its more than five-decade journey in the building materials sector.\n\nThe new outlet, located at No. 85, Dr. N. M. Perera Mawatha in Colombo 08, was unveiled as a modern design destination offering premium wall and floor tile collections, including the company\u2019s signature double-fired tile range.\n\nThe showroom was declared open at a ceremony attended by Chief Guest Chartered Architect Russell Dandeniya and LANKATILES Managing Director Priyantha Talwatte, along with representatives from the architecture, construction and business communities.\n\nPositioned in the Borella area\u2014one of Colombo\u2019s most commercially active and well-connected urban corridors\u2014the new showroom is aimed at serving homeowners, architects, designers and developers seeking contemporary surface solutions.\n\nCompany officials said the expansion reflects a strategic move to align with rapid urban development in the Western Province while improving access to premium design products and services.\n\nSpeaking at the event, Talwatte said the new showroom represents an important step in bringing high-quality tile solutions closer to customers in key urban centres, particularly as Borella evolves into a hub of modern residential and commercial development.\n\nChief Guest Dandeniya, in his remarks, praised the improved quality and customer engagement, noting that the new concept showroom is a valuable addition to Colombo\u2019s growing design landscape.The company said the milestone reinforces its long-standing commitment to innovation, quality and design excellence in Sri Lanka\u2019s construction and interiors sector.\n\nLankan Scout leader Bhanuka Karunaratne first to receive Japan\u2019s Wood Badge\n\nThriposha production hindered amid maize import delay and regulatory impasse"
