    "chunk_text": "The images included in The Ceylon Journal are almost always diligently handpicked before undergoing a process of vetting. It is little doubt that the readers who have given a feedback have often commented on the vitality that it\u2019s images lend to The publication. Illuminating and delightful, they enhance the reading pleasure of its purchasers.\n\nOur little island is regularly one of the top global tourist destinations. One of the immersive experiences it offers are the picturesque train rides for the visitors. After December\u2019s disaster, only 478 km remained operative of the 1,593 km railway network. Time will see it restored back to the former condition. This journal contains the story of how the Uda-Pussellawa railway line came into fruition. It is an engaging article which covers not merely the facts and figures but also explains the context within which the railway line was found to be a necessity. It must also be said that this piece of locomotive history ceased its operations in the year 1948 when Ceylon obtained her independence. Researching on a defunct railway is a taxing endeavor but Prof. Indrani Munasinghe deserves kudos for a job well done and an article well written."
