    "md5": "b47b0c66d116faf3e20428cad9f567f7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1626,
    "chunk_text": "What Bakeer Markar did for Beruwala\n\nMay 12 marked the commemoration of the 109th birth anniversary of Al Haj M.A.Bakeer Markar, who was considered the foremost son of the Beruwala community as he was the pioneer in the development of the Berwala town to what it is today. This account is a dedication to some of his services.\n\nMy memory is awakened on the extensive work done by him as a citizen of Beruwala for the town\u2019s development. After being elected Chairman of the Beruwala Urban Council and later Mayor, it he who laid the foundation to develop the town from a small row of shops to what it is today.\n\nAt the time he became the first citizen of Beruwala, there was no major government building in the town other than that of the Urban Council which preceded the Municipality. It is he who initiated the process of upgrading Beruwala to the status of a separate Divisional Secretariat and the subsequent construction of many imposing buildings in the town.\n\nAt that time there were no shopping complexes, state banks or fisheries offices in Beruwala. Nor did it have a dedicated post office. The were no medical quarters as well.\n\nFrom the first moment he was elected as a Member of Parliament, steps were taken to acquire a large extent of land for the development of Beruwala town. Accordingly, the Divisional Secretariat, the new post office in Beruwala, the Beruwala Youth Vocational Training Center, four medical quarters, the Beruwala Fisheries Complex and other buildings required for the hospital were constructed on acquired land. He had also acquired more land for the future constructions of the hospital."
